question:
What compilation error occurs in the following Java inheritance code?
```java
class Sensor {
    private int reading = 42;
}
class SmartSensor extends Sensor {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println(reading);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program calling an inherited method?
```java
class Vehicle {
    public int speed = 0;
    public void accelerate(int delta) {
        this.speed += delta;
    }
}
class SportsCar extends Vehicle {
    public void turbo() {
        accelerate(50);
    }
}
public class RaceApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SportsCar car = new SportsCar();
        car.accelerate(30);
        car.turbo();
        System.out.println(car.speed);
    }
}
```

What compilation error occurs in the following class declaration extending multiple superclasses?
```java
class Engine {}
class Radio {}
class Automobile extends Engine, Radio {
    int wheels = 4;
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program accessing private state through an inherited public getter?
```java
class Box {
    private int volume = 100;
    public int getVolume() {
        return volume;
    }
}
class GiftBox extends Box {
    public void wrap() {
        System.out.print("Wrapped ");
    }
}
public class PackagingDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        GiftBox gb = new GiftBox();
        gb.wrap();
        System.out.print(gb.getVolume());
    }
}
```

What compilation error occurs in the following Java program attempting to mutate a parent private variable through this?
```java
class Device {
    private int serialId = 1001;
}
class Phone extends Device {
    public void configure(int newId) {
        this.serialId = newId;
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program demonstrating field hiding in an inheritance hierarchy?
```java
class SuperUnit {
    int power = 10;
    public void boost() {
        power += 5;
    }
}
class SubUnit extends SuperUnit {
    int power = 100;
}
public class UnitApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SubUnit sub = new SubUnit();
        sub.boost();
        System.out.println(sub.power + ":" + ((SuperUnit) sub).power);
    }
}
```

What compilation error occurs in the following constructor chaining scenario in an inheritance relationship?
```java
class BaseWorker {
    public BaseWorker(String dept) {}
}
class FieldWorker extends BaseWorker {
    int hours = 40;
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program tracing constructor initialization order in an inheritance chain?
```java
class Alpha {
    public Alpha() {
        System.out.print("A ");
    }
}
class Beta extends Alpha {
    public Beta() {
        System.out.print("B ");
    }
}
class Gamma extends Beta {
    public Gamma() {
        System.out.print("G ");
    }
}
public class HierarchyOrderApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Gamma g = new Gamma();
    }
}
```
